@startuml "Traitement asynchrone des tickets - Diagramme de séquence"

title Génération des billets et envoi d'emails de confirmation

participant "Queue Service\n(Bull/Redis)" as Queue
participant "Ticket Service" as TicketSvc
participant "Email Service" as EmailSvc
participant "Storage" as Storage
participant "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB

== Traitement asynchrone des tickets ==
Queue -> Queue: Process job 'generate-tickets'
Queue -> TicketSvc: generateTicketQRCodes(orderId)
TicketSvc -> DB: SELECT tickets WHERE orderId=?
DB --> TicketSvc: tickets list

loop Pour chaque billet
    TicketSvc -> TicketSvc: generateUniqueQRCode(ticketId)
    TicketSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO qr_codes (ticketId, code, data, generatedAt)
    DB --> TicketSvc: QR code saved
end

TicketSvc -> TicketSvc: generateTicketPDFs(tickets)
TicketSvc -> Storage: Upload PDF files
Storage --> TicketSvc: PDF URLs
TicketSvc -> DB: UPDATE tickets SET pdfUrl=? WHERE id IN (?)

== Envoi de l'email de confirmation ==
Queue -> Queue: Process job 'send-confirmation-email'
Queue -> EmailSvc: sendOrderConfirmation(orderId)
EmailSvc -> DB: SELECT order WITH user, tickets WHERE id=?
DB --> EmailSvc: complete order data

EmailSvc -> EmailSvc: Prepare email template
EmailSvc -> Storage: Download ticket PDFs
Storage --> EmailSvc: PDF attachments
EmailSvc -> EmailSvc: Send SMTP email with attachments
EmailSvc -> DB: INSERT INTO email_logs (type: 'order_confirmation', orderId)

@enduml